From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:44:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: force the USB11 PHY
 session valid

On station boot 2dc6de9f the USB11 host came up, the right port's
switches and VBUS followed an attached drive, and nothing enumerated.
MUSB reported one VBUS error with the session below SessEnd at start and
stayed in a_idle: the PHY's VBUS and session comparators do not see the
port's VBUS, which GPIO94 switches.

The vendor kernel forces those signals at power-on (VBUSVALID, AVALID
and BVALID set, SESSEND clear, all forced) and forces IDDIG low. The
T-PHY's force-b-session-valid forces the same set; the host mode the
MUSB glue sets after power-on then clears IDDIG, giving the vendor's
state.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index 1c6193c9d..473b6bdcd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -800,7 +800,14 @@ &usb11_tphy {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The USB11 PHY's VBUS and session comparators do not see the right
+ * port's VBUS, which GPIO94 switches. As the vendor kernel does, force the
+ * session signals valid; the host mode the glue then sets clears IDDIG, so
+ * the controller is an A-device with VBUS present and starts its session.
+ */
 &usb11_u2 {
+	mediatek,force-b-session-valid;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
